      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for that comment (and whole review), it forces thinking again about all that stuff.\n\nOn few changes which seems to be logic, I responded in the comments below and IMO they are acceptable as refactor. Even if they change a logic in general, they do not change logic in current code usage.\n\nAbout synchronization, I had similar thought even before but at the end I added them because:\n- there is a quite big possibility to add/change some syncHandle variables during clearing them\n- almost all operations in block are synchronize, and it is only about checking local variables so performance downgrade is minimal\n- this will open us to make refactor in the future to collect variables in one object\n- I tested it a lot and did not notice any regression\n- If we merge it without flag, QA will find potential issues much quicker;)",
